# truncation — a value shortened to fit a display is shortened by the renderer
# that knows who is reading, never on the way in.
#
# The surface is derived by internal/surfaceaudit.TruncationSurface: any
# function containing `<something> + <ellipsis>`. Sites are keyed by the
# enclosing function.
#
# Finding #14 reported one site — the log family's message column. There were
# six, in five files, each written from memory in the same shape:
#
#     if len(msg) > 60 { msg = msg[:57] + "..." }
#
# and each doing it while ASSEMBLING a format.Table row, so `--json`, `--full`
# and `--tokensmax 0` were all downstream of the cut and could not undo it. Two
# of the five the report did not name reached a machine: `ent ls --json`
# answered `"state": "2026-07-31T03:13:..."` for 76 of the reference instance's
# 4486 entities while `ent show --json` answered the whole instant for the same
# field, and `trace show --json` carried the last forty characters of a step's
# error. Nothing in the tree could have said how many sites there were.
#
# Routing through format.Clip is how a site leaves this surface, which is why
# the list is four functions rather than ten: the columns that need a width
# DECLARE one now (format.Table.SetWidth) instead of applying it. That is the
# same reduction the clock surface made when five renderers became three.
#
# What this surface does NOT see: a shortening that drops characters without
# marking the cut. It is invisible here and invisible to the H-10 sweep's
# clause (6), which is also written against the marker — and it is a strictly
# worse defect than the one this exists for, since a silently short value reads
# as complete. There is none in the tree today; the honest statement is that
# nothing would catch one.
#
# The ceiling is the number of sites known to be unproven. It may fall without
# ceremony and may only rise by editing this line on purpose.
#ceiling 0

internal/format/format.go:Clip = proven: TestClip_NeverCutsARuneInHalf

internal/cmd/whoresolve.go:truncateUUID = exempt: builds the "who" LABEL for a changes row, not a value; the whole context_user_id is a sibling field of the same JSON object, so nothing the shortening drops is unreachable
internal/haapi/client.go:NewHTTPStatusError = exempt: caps a response body inside an error message, and an error is written to stderr rather than into a document a machine parses
internal/surfaceaudit/invariants.go:truncate = exempt: shortens an invariant's title inside a surface report a developer reads; not product output and never rendered as an answer
